# Flutter & Dart (AMC8 AI Tutor)

## Style & analysis
- Follow [Effective Dart](https://dart.dev/effective-dart) and the project `frontend/analysis_options.yaml` / `flutter_lints` rules.
- Prefer `final` for locals assigned once; use `const` constructors and literals wherever possible.

## Widgets & UI
- Keep `build` methods small; extract private `_FooWidget` classes when a section exceeds ~40 lines or has its own state.
- Use `Theme.of(context).colorScheme` and `TextTheme` — never hard-coded hex colors or font sizes.
- Never perform async work inside `build()`; load data in `initState`, a controller, or via `FutureBuilder`/`StreamBuilder`.

## State & async
- Use `async`/`await` with explicit `try`/`catch` for all I/O and network calls.
- Keep navigation, dialog, and snackbar calls out of pure data-parsing helpers.
- Use `dio` for HTTP calls to the FastAPI backend; centralise base URL and auth header injection in a single client helper in `frontend/lib/services/`.

## Data & persistence (offline-first)
- This app is offline-first: all question data and user results are cached in SQLite (`sqflite`); the backend is the source of truth but must not be required for practice.
- Wrap multi-row writes (save session + answers) in a `transaction()`; never leave partial writes on failure.
- Sync results to the backend after a test session completes; surface sync failures with a non-intrusive retry UI rather than blocking the user.
- Never block the UI isolate with heavy queries; use `compute()` for large data processing.

## Test session logic
- A test session has exactly two modes: **unlimited** (no timer) and **timed** (standard AMC8: 40 minutes, 25 questions).
- Encapsulate session state (current question index, elapsed time, answers map, mode) in a dedicated model/controller class — not as ad-hoc widget fields.
- The countdown timer must survive widget rebuilds; drive it from a controller that is disposed in `dispose()`.
- On session completion, immediately persist the result to SQLite before any navigation.

## Wrong answer & review lists
- A question can be in the wrong-answer list, the review-marked list, or both simultaneously — model this correctly in the DB and UI.
- Re-test mode must support selecting from wrong answers, review marks, or any combination; pass the selected question IDs as a list, not a filter string.

## User management
- After login, cache the user profile (name, email, phone, language) in SQLite for offline display.
- Profile updates must be sent to the backend; only commit the local cache after a successful API response.
- Language preference (`AppLanguage.code`) is part of the user profile and must be persisted across app restarts — see `i18n-flutter.mdc`.

## Platform
- When changing native permissions or icons, edit `android/` and `ios/` together and document non-obvious reasons in a code comment.
